cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the QVF format or this toolkit, please cite it as below."
title: "QVF: the Quantum Visualization Format — specification and reference implementation"
abstract: >
  QVF is an open container format for quantum-chemistry visualization and
  analysis data: a zip archive with a typed, versioned JSON manifest and
  per-section payloads. This repository carries the normative
  specification, the JSON schema, the registry of canonical section
  kinds, a conformance corpus, and reference writer/reader
  implementations in Python and zero-dependency C++17 with a C ABI. It is
  licensed Apache-2.0 so that any code can adopt the format without
  adopting vibe-qc.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peintinger
    given-names: Michael F.
    website: "https://vibe-qc.com/"
version: 0.1.0
url: "https://vibe-qc.com/docs/qvf/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vibe-qc/qvf"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - file format
  - quantum chemistry
  - interoperability
  - wavefunction
